# A push of the commit a green `pnpm check` stamped, on a clean tree, skips check:fast: check ran all of it already
# (scripts/check-stamp.mjs, fix/pre-push-stamp). So does a push that does not update main of the commit a green
# default `pnpm check:changed` stamped, and the Steward's push of a quest or train branch at the commit its checks
# passed on, named in ELVARIA_CHECKED_HEAD (RC-01). Any doubt runs check:fast. pnpm is called here, from sh, because
# Node would need a shell to start pnpm.cmd on Windows (ADR 0015).
node scripts/check-stamp.mjs verify || pnpm check:fast
